## Baseline Timing Results (median of 3 runs, batch_size=8)

| Phase | Median (ms) |
|-------|-------------|
| Model loading | 12,880 |
| Frame extraction (ffmpeg) | 6,319 |
| Whisper audio features | 39 |
| Face detect + landmarks | 19,840 |
| VAE encode (all frames) | 3,918 |
| **UNet total** | **5,445** |
| UNet per frame | 3.6 |
| UNet median batch (8 frames) | 28.2 |
| **VAE decode total** | **12,679** |
| VAE decode per frame | 8.5 |
| **Blending total** | **74,574** |
| Blending per frame | 49.7 |
| **TOTAL PIPELINE** | **138,016** |
| Effective FPS | 10.9 |
| VRAM peak | 36,157 MB |

**Key insight:** Blending (49.7ms/frame) dominates per-frame cost, not UNet (3.6ms) or VAE decode (8.5ms). This aligns with Taiboli's finding that the render path isn't the bottleneck.

## Noise Floor

Pipeline is **fully deterministic** — 1500/1500 frames bit-identical across runs. Any PSNR < inf after an optimization is a REAL quality regression, not measurement noise.

